                "username": "zyxiaooo"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "I wouldn't complicate this to have multiple states, just always advertise the best source address for the current default gateway. If it's missing, fall back to the older behavior as that either means no real default is available or the CNBMC is old."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yuxiao Zhang",
                        "email": "yuxiaozhang@google.com",
                        "username": "zyxiaooo"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 199,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "If you are going to do this you need to keep track of the metrics and srcs and maintain a dict to keep track of them as they change. You need to pick the best one to make a source route for regardless of the order they are discovered / go away. That way you can fall back to the NCSI port here when the front panel goes away. We can't just ignore sending the NCSI address because we should send the right ones. If we have a default gateway, we should send the route."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 199,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yuxiao Zhang",
                        "email": "yuxiaozhang@google.com",
                        "username": "zyxiaooo"
                    },
                    "message": "I think only this hybrid oob ip will use this special /124 address, all other addresses will be unaffected by this so there is no need to make this channel universal for all types of addresses?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-google/networking/gbmc-bridge/gbmc-br-gw-src.sh",
                    "line": 199,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yuxiao Zhang",
                        "email": "yuxiaozhang@google.com",
                        "username": "zyxiaooo"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Now just sending the highest metric route"
                }
            ],
